.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt POLICYCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm policyctl
.Nd validate and inspect capability principal policy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Nm
.Cm validate | format
.Ar file
.Nm
.Cm explain
.Ar file user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
uses the same principal-policy parser as BSDAuth.
.Cm init
prints an empty, least-privilege policy suitable for editing.
.Cm validate
checks the complete document, including entries that do not match a user.
.Cm format
prints the validated document as JSON, preserving policy entry order.
.Cm explain
prints the grants for a named account using the current system's user and
group databases; it does not inspect a running session or change authority.
For an offline boot environment, run it within that environment so account
resolution uses the matching databases.
.Pp
Input must be a bounded regular file; symbolic links are refused.
Validation checks syntax and schema, not ownership, executable integrity,
boot selection, or whether requested endpoints exist.
.Pp
Persistent principal policy is loaded into an immutable snapshot by BSDAuth
at startup.
Editing or replacing its file does not revoke existing grants or
change the loaded snapshot.
Stage policy with its matching system in an
inactive boot environment and reboot to activate it.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Invalid policy or an unavailable account returns 2.
Invalid command usage returns 64.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bectl 8 ,
.Xr BSDAuth 8
